 ## Overview
-Lanczos resampling is an interpolation technique used to resample (downsample or upsample) volumetric data by replacing each selected sample with a translated copy of the Lanczos kernel, which is a limited Sinc function [S1, unofficial]. It is chosen when high-frequency detail preservation is required, such as in medical image compression and reconstruction [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from its siblings, such as [Interpolation Schemes for Volume Rendering](817-interpolation-schemes-for-volume-rendering.md) and [Interpolation Functions for Resampling](15932-interpolation-functions-for-resampling.md), by applying a windowed sinc kernel to balance sharpness and aliasing suppression.
